<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rotrou III, Count of Perche</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1144</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Rotrou the Great</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rotrou III was Count of Perche from about 1100 to 1144 and a leading crusader. He took part in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-crusade">First Crusade</a>, then fought for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-i-of-aragon">Alfonso I of Aragon</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almoravid-empire">Almoravids</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ebro-river">Ebro</a> valley, receiving the lordship of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tudela">Tudela</a>. He married Matilda, an illegitimate daughter of Henry I of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, and died in 1144 of wounds received at the siege of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rouen">Rouen</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rotrou-iii-count-of-perche.jpg" alt="Rotrou III, Count of Perche" width="320" height="314" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 1895 Joseph-Hector-Henri-Jean Guillier de Souancé · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rotrou_III.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
